Oliver Day is a Nephilim of [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]]'s research department, red-skinned and horned, with goat's eyes and hooves. He was aboard the [[Geography/Færrin/Infinite Horizon/Far Realms/Hesperid|Hesperid]] when it struck the ascending [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Gremory]], and the collision shut him inside a shelter on the ship's bridge floor, where he lived some thirty years on berries he grows by magic, until the shelter was opened and he was brought out.

He knows the wreck's workings. Every shelter but his own stayed sealed on the inside, and the sealed rooms open to a key cut in Sedecium's sixteen-pointed star. The great door at the foot of the elevator shaft is a one-way passage into the engine room, and the magic that fills it can be passed only by a body falling from high enough under a rite of heat-shielding, such as Oliver can cast. He is of the research staff, no captain, and cannot steer the ship. His own piece of the star-key he left behind in his office in the dormitory.

He was the highest-ranked of the four Sedecium survivors aboard when he came out, and the others fell back under his lead. Nothing much rattles him; he stayed unbothered while the Protectorate met the returning train at gunpoint and the other three went pale. He has the run of the Party's workshop aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] now, and is building there the communications array he means to use to reach [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]].
